# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sierra-III: what never goes into this repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Game data. Nothing that comes from the game files, ever: no maps, no
#    extracted tags, no baked packs. Everyone bakes their own from their own
#    disc with bake/halo-psp-bake.
*.map
*.pgeo
*.ptex
*.pstn
*.adp
*.vram
*.xbe
*.iso
*.bik
*.xmv
*.wma
*.xma
/maps/
/tags/
*_tags/
tags_*/
**/halo/maps/
# Tag files by extension (what Invader or the HEK extract)
*.bitmap
*.sound
*.scenario
*.scenario_structure_bsp
*.gbxmodel
*.model_animations
*.model_collision_geometry
*.shader_*
*.unicode_string_list
*.font
# Audio clipped from the game's music (e.g. for the XMB's SND0). Keep these
# local and pack them with PSP_XMB_SND0; see psp/xmb/README.md.
*.at3
*.AT3
/psp/xmb/local/

# 2. Build output. psp_build.py regenerates all of it.
/build/
**/build/
**/build2/
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.prx
*.PBP
*.SFO
*.map.txt
halo.map
/link/objs.rsp
/link/stubs.c
/link/stubbed_symbols.txt
# a bake run from this checkout: what the guided bake and the installer make
/bake/COPY-TO-MEMORY-STICK/
/bake/out/

# 3. Firmware or other third-party binaries (never ours to publish).
flash0/
*.bin

# 4. Hardware logs and emulator runs: never committed.
/logs/
/runs/
*.tgz
*.zip
# ...but the profile-guided build's counts are ours (counts of this code's
# branches, no game data): psp_build.py reads them from pgo/
!/pgo/*.tgz

# 5. Python and editor clutter.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.swp
.DS_Store
